---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import PageShell from '../../../../components/PageShell.astro';
import { person } from '../../../../data/cv';
import { withBase } from '../../../../utils/paths';

const title = `Understanding Journals and Indexes · Doing Research · ${person.fullDisplayName}`;
const description = 'Learn to read a journal homepage, verify indexing, interpret journal metrics and quartiles, and check publication requirements.';
const journals = [
  { name: 'Language Testing', publisher: 'Sage', focus: 'Language assessment research', href: 'https://journals.sagepub.com/home/ltj' },
  { name: 'Language Assessment Quarterly', publisher: 'Taylor & Francis / Routledge', focus: 'Language assessment theory and practice', href: 'https://www.tandfonline.com/toc/hlaq20/current' },
  { name: 'Assessing Writing', publisher: 'Elsevier', focus: 'Writing assessment', href: 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/journal/assessing-writing' },
  { name: 'Language Testing in Asia', publisher: 'Springer Nature', focus: 'Language assessment in Asia and the Asia-Pacific region', href: 'https://link.springer.com/journal/40468' },
  { name: 'Language Education & Assessment', publisher: 'Castledown', focus: 'Second / foreign language education and assessment', href: 'https://www.castledown.com/journals/lea/' },
];
const homepageChecks = [
  { label: 'Aims & scope · 宗旨與範圍', question: 'Does my study fit the journal?', evidence: 'Match the research problem, audience, article type and contribution to the stated scope. Explain the connection rather than relying on a shared keyword.' },
  { label: 'Indexing · 收錄情況', question: 'Where is the journal indexed?', evidence: 'Record the exact index and coverage status. Verify the journal title and ISSN in the database provider’s own journal list.' },
  { label: 'Metrics · 期刊指標', question: 'What does the reported number mean?', evidence: 'Record the metric name, metric year, subject category and rank or percentile. A single impact score does not establish a quartile.' },
  { label: 'Review speed · 審稿時間', question: 'What stage does the time estimate describe?', evidence: 'Distinguish first editorial decision, peer-review decision, acceptance and online publication. Published averages or medians are estimates, not a promise for your manuscript.' },
  { label: 'Publishing options · 出版模式', question: 'What route and costs are available?', evidence: 'Check subscription, hybrid or fully open access options; APCs, other charges, waivers, institutional agreements and funder requirements.' },
  { label: 'Author guidelines · 作者指南', question: 'What must I prepare before submitting?', evidence: 'Check word limits, article types, reference style, tables and figures, anonymisation, ethics statements and required submission files.' },
  { label: 'Editors & recent articles · 編委與近期文章', question: 'Who reads and publishes work here?', evidence: 'Review the editorial board’s expertise and the last 5–10 articles. Look for relevant methods, topics and contributions as evidence of fit.' },
];
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description}>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main-content" class="min-h-[50vh] w-full bg-page">
    <PageShell accentBar>
      <div class="journal-topic max-w-5xl">
        <p class="type-label text-secondary">Doing Research · Topic 1</p>
        <h1 class="mt-2 font-serif text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl">Understanding Journals and Indexes</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-secondary" lang="zh-Hant">認識期刊與學術索引</p>
        <p class="type-intro mt-4">Read a journal’s publishing information and use evidence to decide whether it is a suitable home for your research.</p>
        <nav class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-2 text-sm" aria-label="Topic sections">
          <a href="#journals">Journal examples</a><a href="#homepage">Reading a homepage</a><a href="#indexes">Indexes</a><a href="#metrics">Metrics & quartiles</a><a href="#publishing">Costs & requirements</a><a href="#journal-audit">Journal audit</a>
        </nav>

        <section id="journals" class="topic-section" aria-labelledby="journals-heading">
          <h2 id="journals-heading">1. Know the journal and its publisher</h2>
          <p>A journal publishes a particular body of scholarly work. A publisher may run many journals with different scopes and requirements. Start with the official homepage of the individual journal.</p>
          <div class="table-scroll">
            <table>
              <caption class="sr-only">Journal examples from the Week 1 materials</caption>
              <thead><tr><th scope="col">Journal</th><th scope="col">Publisher</th><th scope="col">Area to explore</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>{journals.map((journal) => <tr><th scope="row"><a href={journal.href}>{journal.name}</a></th><td>{journal.publisher}</td><td>{journal.focus}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted">These are examples for exploration. Check current indexing, metrics and fees separately for each journal.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="homepage" class="topic-section" aria-labelledby="homepage-heading">
          <h2 id="homepage-heading">2. Read a journal homepage with a purpose</h2>
          <p>Open one journal above. For each question, find the relevant page and record the evidence that informs your decision.</p>
          <dl class="homepage-checks">
            {homepageChecks.map((check) => <div><dt>{check.label}</dt><dd><strong>{check.question}</strong><p>{check.evidence}</p></dd></div>)}
          </dl>
          <p>For example, a study of AI scoring in speaking assessment needs an explanation of how its contribution fits the journal’s assessment interests. A keyword missing from the scope is a reason to investigate further; it does not by itself establish an automatic rejection.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="indexes" class="topic-section" aria-labelledby="indexes-heading">
          <h2 id="indexes-heading">3. Understand academic indexes</h2>
          <p>Citation indexes help researchers discover publications and trace citations. Indexing, a journal’s citation metrics and an institution’s publication requirements are separate things to check.</p>
          <div class="table-scroll">
            <table>
              <caption class="sr-only">Major indexes introduced in this topic</caption>
              <thead><tr><th scope="col">Index</th><th scope="col">Full name</th><th scope="col">Context</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><th scope="row">SSCI</th><td>Social Sciences Citation Index<br /><span lang="zh-Hant">社會科學引文索引</span></td><td>Social sciences, including education and linguistics; part of the Web of Science Core Collection.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">SCIE</th><td>Science Citation Index Expanded<br /><span lang="zh-Hant">科學引文索引擴展版</span></td><td>Science disciplines; part of the Web of Science Core Collection.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">A&HCI</th><td>Arts & Humanities Citation Index<br /><span lang="zh-Hant">藝術與人文引文索引</span></td><td>Arts and humanities; part of the Web of Science Core Collection.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">ESCI</th><td>Emerging Sources Citation Index<br /><span lang="zh-Hant">新興來源引文索引</span></td><td>A Web of Science Core Collection index covering journals that meet Clarivate’s quality criteria.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Scopus</th><td>Elsevier’s abstract and citation database</td><td>Multidisciplinary coverage. Scopus indexing does not establish SSCI indexing.</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p>SSCI, SCIE, A&HCI and ESCI belong to the same Core Collection but have distinct coverage. ESCI is not a guarantee of later transfer to SSCI or SCIE. Journals can change coverage following re-evaluation.</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted">Check the <a href="https://mjl.clarivate.com/">Clarivate Master Journal List</a> and <a href="https://www.scopus.com/sources">Scopus Sources</a> by title or ISSN. Read the <a href="https://clarivate.com/academia-government/scientific-and-academic-research/research-discovery-and-referencing/web-of-science/web-of-science-core-collection/editorial-selection-process/journal-evaluation-process-selection-criteria/">Clarivate selection criteria</a> for the relationship between these collections.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="metrics" class="topic-section" aria-labelledby="metrics-heading">
          <h2 id="metrics-heading">4. Read metrics and quartiles carefully</h2>
          <div class="table-scroll">
            <table>
              <caption class="sr-only">Comparison of journal metrics and ranking systems</caption>
              <thead><tr><th scope="col">Metric or system</th><th scope="col">What it describes</th><th scope="col">What to record</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><th scope="row">Journal Impact Factor (JIF)</th><td>A JCR citation measure: citations in the metric year to items from the preceding two years, divided by the eligible scholarly items published in those two years.</td><td>JIF year, subject category and the reported JIF rank / quartile.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Journal Citation Indicator (JCI)</th><td>A JCR measure of citation impact normalised by subject category, document type and publication year.</td><td>The named JCI measure and year. Keep JCI and JIF rankings distinct.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">CiteScore</th><td>A Scopus measure using citations and eligible documents within the same four-year window.</td><td>CiteScore year, subject category, rank and percentile / quartile.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">CAS journal partition<br /><span lang="zh-Hant">中科院期刊分區</span></th><td>A separate classification published by the Chinese Academy of Sciences Documentation and Information Center.</td><td>Edition / year, broad or narrow subject category, and the reported partition (1–4).</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p>A quartile describes a journal’s relative position within a specified subject category. Q1 indicates the highest quarter of the ranking, followed by Q2, Q3 and Q4. Use the provider’s reported quartile, including its handling of ties and categories.</p>
          <p>The same journal may have different quartiles across categories, years or metric systems. “Q1” alone is incomplete: write the system, metric year and category. CAS partitions use their own methodology and must be looked up separately.</p>
          <p class="metric-example"><strong>Reporting pattern:</strong> [Journal title] · [JCR JIF / Scopus CiteScore] · [metric year] · [subject category] · [rank or percentile] · [reported quartile].</p>
          <p>Having a JIF does not establish SSCI coverage: ESCI journals also receive a JIF. Use journal metrics alongside scope, readership and recent publications when choosing a journal.</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted">Official guidance: <a href="https://webofscience.help.clarivate.com/en-us/Content/wos-core-collection/wos-full-record.htm">JIF definition</a>, <a href="https://clarivate.com/download/introducing-the-journal-citation-indicator/">JCI explanation</a>, <a href="https://service.elsevier.com/app/answers/detail/a_id/14880/supporthub/scopus/">CiteScore methodology</a>, <a href="https://www.fenqubiao.com/">CAS journal partition platform</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="publishing" class="topic-section" aria-labelledby="publishing-heading">
          <h2 id="publishing-heading">5. Check costs, timing and submission requirements</h2>
          <h3>Publishing route and fees · 出版模式與費用</h3>
          <p>A subscription journal restricts reader access; a hybrid journal offers both subscription and open access publication; a fully open access journal makes its articles openly available. Open access may involve an article processing charge (APC), but fees, waivers and institutional agreements vary.</p>
          <p>Record the current fee, currency, taxes and funding options from the journal’s official page. Also check page, colour or other charges. A subscription route can still have charges, and the label “open access” does not tell you what you personally must pay. See <a href="https://support.springernature.com/en/support/solutions/articles/6000084580-costs-of-publishing-in-springer-nature-journal">Springer Nature’s costs guidance</a> and its <a href="https://stories.springernature.com/apcguide/index.html">APC and funding guide</a>.</p>
          <h3>Review timing · 審稿時間</h3>
          <p>“Time to first decision” may include decisions made before external peer review. It is not the same as time to acceptance. Read the definition of each statistic and allow time for revision when planning around a deadline.</p>
          <h3>Author guidelines · 投稿指南</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Length:</strong> check the word limit and whether references, tables, captions and appendices count.</li>
            <li><strong>Style:</strong> check the required reference and manuscript format.</li>
            <li><strong>Review model:</strong> for anonymous review, follow the journal’s instructions for separating author details and removing identifying information.</li>
            <li><strong>Required files:</strong> confirm the title page, main manuscript, figures, supplementary materials and declarations requested by the journal.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="journal-audit" class="topic-section" aria-labelledby="audit-heading">
          <h2 id="audit-heading">6. Try it: build a journal profile</h2>
          <p>Choose two journals relevant to your research. Compare the following evidence before deciding which is a better fit.</p>
          <ol>
            <li><strong>Identity:</strong> journal title, publisher, ISSN and official homepage.</li>
            <li><strong>Fit:</strong> one sentence connecting your research to the scope, supported by two recent articles.</li>
            <li><strong>Indexing:</strong> exact index, provider record, coverage status and date checked.</li>
            <li><strong>Metrics:</strong> named metric, metric year, subject category and reported rank / quartile.</li>
            <li><strong>Practical requirements:</strong> word limit, review model, publishing route, current costs and timing information.</li>
            <li><strong>Decision:</strong> explain the strongest reason for your choice and one point that still needs checking.</li>
          </ol>
          <details class="mt-5 border-y border-border py-3">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer text-base font-semibold text-ink">Check your understanding: three claims to question</summary>
            <dl class="mt-3 space-y-3">
              <div><dt class="font-semibold">“This journal has an Impact Factor, so it is SSCI.”</dt><dd>Check the index itself. ESCI journals can also have a JIF.</dd></div>
              <div><dt class="font-semibold">“It is Q1, so it must be the best journal for my paper.”</dt><dd>Identify the system, year and category, then assess scope, audience and manuscript fit.</dd></div>
              <div><dt class="font-semibold">“The first decision takes 24 days, so my article will be accepted in 24 days.”</dt><dd>A first decision is a different stage from acceptance and can occur before external peer review.</dd></div>
            </dl>
          </details>
        </section>

        <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-muted">Adapted from April Jiawei Zhang’s DEDC02 Week 1 materials (25 August 2026), slides 12–23. Index and metric explanations are supplemented by the official resources linked above. Check current journal records when applying this guidance.</p>
        <a href={withBase('/teaching/training/doing-research')} class="mt-8 inline-flex text-sm font-semibold">← All Doing Research topics</a>
      </div>
    </PageShell>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .topic-section { margin-top: 2rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); scroll-margin-top: 5rem; }
  .topic-section h2 { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.3; color: var(--color-ink); }
  .topic-section h3 { margin-top: 1.25rem; font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-ink); }
  .topic-section p { margin-top: .75rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .topic-section ul, .topic-section ol { margin-top: .75rem; padding-left: 1.25rem; }
  .topic-section ul { list-style: disc; }
  .topic-section ol { list-style: decimal; }
  .topic-section li + li { margin-top: .5rem; }
  .table-scroll { margin: 1rem 0; overflow-x: auto; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .9375rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  th, td { padding: .75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  thead { background: var(--color-main-faint); }
  th { font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-ink); }
  th:first-child { min-width: 10rem; }
  .homepage-checks { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .homepage-checks > div { padding: .85rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(10rem, 1fr) 3fr; gap: 1rem; }
  .homepage-checks dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-secondary); }
  .homepage-checks dd p { margin-top: .25rem; }
  .metric-example { border-left: 3px solid var(--color-secondary); padding-left: 1rem; }
  @media (max-width: 639px) { .homepage-checks > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: .3rem; } th, td { padding: .65rem; } }
</style>
